{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, this yoke is after freezing on me again. Give me two seconds. Right, what has you in?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): I'm just wrecked, doctor. Tired all the time, and cold with it. I don't know, I put it down to work and getting older.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): Tired and cold. Say that again, I was in the wrong tab. How long is the tiredness going on?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): A few months. Three months... no, it's six months, since after Christmas. I don't know, doctor, the days all blur.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She's perished in the house. The heating's up full and she's still in a jumper.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): And I'm after putting on weight. The bowels have gone slow as well, I'm constipated, and that was never me.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right. Constipation, weight up. And the mood? You look a bit flat, but tell me yourself.",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): The mood is low, yeah. Not crying or anything. Just flat. I blamed the job, to be honest.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She manages a shop out in the retail park. Long days, on her feet. She's fifty-two.",
  "[SEG0010] person_1 (DOCTOR): Fifty-two, shop manager. Grand. The medication list is taking its time. Are you on anything regular?",
  "[SEG0011] person_4 (NURSE): I have it here from the chart. Atorvastatin twenty milligrams, one at night.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): That's not right. They put me up to forty. I'm on the forty milligram tablets.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): The box in the press at home still says twenty. I don't think you ever started the higher ones.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know, doctor. Maybe I didn't. The packets all look the same to me.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, say the dose again? I was half reading a letter. The list says twenty and you're saying forty.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): I think they said forty. I don't know.",
  "[SEG0017] person_4 (NURSE): Weight on the way in was eighty-two kilos. Blood pressure one-eighteen over seventy-six... no, sorry, wrong line, it's one thirty-four over eighty-two. Pulse sixty-eight.",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (DOCTOR): One thirty-four over eighty-two, pulse sixty-eight, eighty-two kilos. Any chest pain, or trouble with the breathing?",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Nothing like that.",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (DOCTOR): And palpitations? Heart going fast?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): No, I don't think so.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Her mother had thyroid trouble. Underactive. On the tablets for years.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Mother had an underactive thyroid. Did anyone ever check yours?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): Years ago, yeah. They said it was borderline. I don't know, doctor, that's what I remember.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Borderline. Hang on, the results are slow to open. Can you say that again, borderline when?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): I haven't a clue when. Ages ago. I don't know.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): The TSH on the file is 1.8. That's normal, not borderline at all. You might be mixing it up.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): Oh. Right. Maybe that was my mother, so. I don't know.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): Apart from the constipation, any sickness, or pain in the tummy?",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): No sickness. No pain. Just the slow bowels.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): And the waterworks, all grand?",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Grand, yeah.",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She lives on tea, mind. Barely touches water.",
  "[SEG0034] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'm thinking this may be an underactive thyroid. The cold, the tiredness, the weight, the bowels. Not sure until the bloods are back.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): Would that not have shown up before? I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (DOCTOR): The old test was normal. These things can change. I'll send you for bloods, thyroid function and a full blood count.",
  "[SEG0037] person_4 (NURSE): I can take the bloods down the corridor after ye're done, if you want them today.",
  "[SEG0038] person_1 (DOCTOR): Yes, today. And come back to me next week for the results, whether they're up or down.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): Grand. Next week so. Thanks, doctor."
 ],
